<title>USA: Mercury Air sees 97 revs up to $300 mln.</title>
<headline>Mercury Air sees 97 revs up to $300 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercury Air Group Inc said it expects consolidated revenues to reach about $300 million in fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>The aviation services company posted $225.4 million in revenues in fiscal 1996.  Mercury also expects EBITDA to reach about $16 million in fiscal 1997, up from $12.4 million in 1996, said Seymour Kahn, Mercury Air chief executive.</p>
<p>Speaking at the Dillon Read Airlines, Aviation Services and Logistics Conference, Kahn declined to comment on earnings, saying fluctuating fuel prices made estimates difficult to provide.</p>
</text>
